      {
        "number": 8,
        "internalPageId": null,
        "title": "We use relative clauses or relative pronouns to include extra information about someone or something in the sentences.",
        "visibleTexts": [
          "We use relative clauses or relative pronouns to include extra information about someone or something in the sentences.",
          "About... Words Examples People Who Jake, who is the GOAT athlete, is here. Places Where The club, where Sarah went legless, is closing. Things Which The house, which the busybody bought, is great. Time When Tonight, when I see my jellybean, I’ll confess my love. Reasons Why I don’t know why he is so wishy-washy about this. Belonging Whose Joe, whose party was so dismal, has another one this weekend.",
          "To consider",
          "1. Most relative pronouns are enclosed between commas. 2. They can also be used as the example with why. 3. How can be used to set clauses related to manners or ways. E.G: I know how he did it!",
          "4. We can also used that to create relative clauses for people and things. Jane, that lives here, is my best friend. The car, that is on the corner, was stolen yesterday."
        ],
        "links": [],
        "media": [
          {
            "url": "https://docs.google.com/slides-images-rt/AE1YXSbrR9WhTLf-CK_s3y3J9R1Zsga6VWtv1lWbstP79r0Z5i--Ob7mOe9SojQ1Y40WLhFnhyeK8VanOYG8ju-0l78xNuBjtF12ZUWxZbI81rtgwhq5rp8ud8j_8ub7IhnbuP1v_P4OBWgdfjENWSzSWT76IYHCqbCyK5icVJsntH537sgSSvlQT0NFdU45fwbsUA=s2048",
